{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs","id":1205901,"title":"(2e) Would it break the setting if DBs could enlighten into CCS...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-11T20:50:03-07:00","id":1205901,"title":"(2e) Would it break the setting if DBs could enlighten into CCS...","content":"...but because no organization had ever considered instilling them with that power a priority, no standardized path to that type of enlightenment existed?<br /> IE, very rare beings like Her Redness and Mnemon initiate into CCS (with the Mantle of Brigid here being an inspiration or implement for that, rather than the source of it), but there is no pair of charms like Tiger and Bear, the Irises path, the Immaculate enlightening charms, or even that thaumaturgy that lets you enlighten into CCS through a number of years of asceticism. Every DB who breaks that barrier has to make their own path, which generally demands it's own sacrifices, before they're prepared to initiate into the step above.<br /> <br /> Because really, the idea that DBs with CCS are possible, but nobody has ever created a standard way to prepare one's mind to receive that enlightenment because nobody ever felt they needed/should have that power is more reasonable to me than &quot;DB martial artists can reach a tier above with difficulty, but FUCK DB sorcerers - their horizons stretch basically no further than mortals&quot;. After all, the standardized methods for them to reach CMA all stem back to the Deliberative wanting more effective DB lieutenants and soldiers. Maybe it's just that nobody <i>cared</i> about DB CCS, and Salina was too focused on bringing sorcery to EVERYONE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","user":"PlotVitalNPC","date":". 04-11-2018, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T21:45:04-07:00","id":1205910,"title":"","content":"Well there was that incident where a sid tried to teach SMA to a DB and the end result was the DB going boom. <br /> <br /> I mean if you treat it as exceptionally difficult, or requires other things then it should be fine. I mean if you play it as, &quot;Oh yeah all the Dragonblood can reach Celestial sorcery they've just never tried hard enough.&quot; then its a problem.<br /> <br /> If its something like, &quot;There are individuals, rare, difficult to find, but they do exist among the Dragonblood that can attain this power. Of course the only way to tell if one is capable of this feat is to actually succeed at the endeavor and there isn't really a sign that it will happen until it does. They say the ritual needed is different for each that attempts and succeeds, but it is never easy. That plus all the effort and various rituals or components supposedly needed to access it means that most do not attempt lest they spend ages futily searching for the right combination of components and meditations to get something that may not even be accessible to them.&quot; Everything is probably fine then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:00:48-07:00","id":1205917,"title":"","content":"It seems likely that various Exalted over the millennia would have thought that Dragon-Blooded should have that level of power, and would have tried to draw it out. Now, if it's possible and people just didn't know <i>how</i>, that's &quot;setting breaking&quot; in a way that could made for a good campaign hook. Otherwise, I think it works best as a benefit from an N/A Artifact or incredibly ambitious working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:33:37-07:00","id":1205928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1205910#post1205910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there was that incident where a sid tried to teach SMA to a DB and the end result was the DB going boom. <br /> <br /> I mean if you treat it as exceptionally difficult, or requires other things then it should be fine. I mean if you play it as, &quot;Oh yeah all the Dragonblood can reach Celestial sorcery they've just never tried hard enough.&quot; then its a problem.<br /> <br /> If its something like, &quot;There are individuals, rare, difficult to find, but they do exist among the Dragonblood that can attain this power. Of course the only way to tell if one is capable of this feat is to actually succeed at the endeavor and there isn't really a sign that it will happen until it does. They say the ritual needed is different for each that attempts and succeeds, but it is never easy. That plus all the effort and various rituals or components supposedly needed to access it means that most do not attempt lest they spend ages futily searching for the right combination of components and meditations to get something that may not even be accessible to them.&quot; Everything is probably fine then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps CCS is part of what you get when you purchase Essence 10 and the 5th purchase of Transcendent Gaian Harmony?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or, more accurately, it\u2019s what you evolve into gets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-12-2018, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T23:06:39-07:00","id":1205945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1205917#post1205917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems likely that various Exalted over the millennia would have thought that Dragon-Blooded should have that level of power, and would have tried to draw it out. Now, if it's possible and people just didn't know <i>how</i>, that's &quot;setting breaking&quot; in a way that could made for a good campaign hook. Otherwise, I think it works best as a benefit from an N/A Artifact or incredibly ambitious working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I'm planning on it, but if I was going to introduce Celestial Circle Sorcery on a DB with would be through a custom artifact. <i>Overwhelming Pendant of the Sun</i> or something, and it should have a significant drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T00:09:24-07:00","id":1205958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1205928#post1205928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps CCS is part of what you get when you purchase Essence 10 and the 5th purchase of Transcendent Gaian Harmony?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or, more accurately, it\u2019s what you evolve into gets?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, I couldn't say since I don't know that charm and well this would very much be a houseruling scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T08:20:52-07:00","id":1206032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1205910#post1205910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there was that incident where a sid tried to teach SMA to a DB and the end result was the DB going boom.<br /> <br /> I mean if you treat it as exceptionally difficult, or requires other things then it should be fine. I mean if you play it as, &quot;Oh yeah all the Dragonblood can reach Celestial sorcery they've just never tried hard enough.&quot; then its a problem.<br /> <br /> If its something like, &quot;There are individuals, rare, difficult to find, but they do exist among the Dragonblood that can attain this power. Of course the only way to tell if one is capable of this feat is to actually succeed at the endeavor and there isn't really a sign that it will happen until it does. They say the ritual needed is different for each that attempts and succeeds, but it is never easy. That plus all the effort and various rituals or components supposedly needed to access it means that most do not attempt lest they spend ages futily searching for the right combination of components and meditations to get something that may not even be accessible to them.&quot; Everything is probably fine then.</div> </div> </div> </div>My premise wasn't that <i>they</i> never tried hard enough, but rather <i>there was never sufficient external support </i>to develop a universal method. The first methods to reach CMA as a DB no matter who you are were developed with the support of a large part of the Deliberative, who were seeking to augment the efficacy of the DBs as warriors. Those same people, or even just some of them, may have considered it not worth it to make DBs celestial circle sorcerers, in such a way that it totally killed the project to develop a universally accessible path to CCS for them.<br /> <br /> Or rather, 'Discovering the first method which allowed <i>every </i>DB to reach CMA if they got the right tuition canonically required the effort of the most powerful nation in the setting, which could probably work with a number of DB sorcerers larger than the current amount of DBs.' There's no reason to assume creating a universal method for celestial circle sorcerers would be less demanding.<br /> <br /> Heck, maybe there's a method that was lost to the depths of time that can enlighten some arbitrary subset of DBs, but not all of them - and which was lost, because over time it failed so often that it was considered something no better than normal, or because it failed to meet the needs of the over-ambitious process that sought to create it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1205917#post1205917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems likely that various Exalted over the millennia would have thought that Dragon-Blooded should have that level of power, and would have tried to draw it out. Now, if it's possible and people just didn't know <i>how</i>, that's &quot;setting breaking&quot; in a way that could made for a good campaign hook. Otherwise, I think it works best as a benefit from an N/A Artifact or incredibly ambitious working.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e, sorcerous workings aren't a mechanical thing, even though CLEARLY given the Salinan working they're some manner of lore thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1205928#post1205928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps CCS is part of what you get when you purchase Essence 10 and the 5th purchase of Transcendent Gaian Harmony?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or, more accurately, it\u2019s what you evolve into gets?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's asking WAY more of them than reaching CMA asks, when fundamentally they're not getting much more. My premise here is that there is no reason CCS should be any more metaphysically out of their reach than CMA, aside from the sheer amount of outside effort that was originally, canonically invested in allowing them access to CMA.<br /> I mean, sure, it might do that, but I wouldn't want that to be their only way to it, because it preserves the really weird dichotomy here. &quot;It's possible to create a method by which anyone can enlighten into it if they're, like, essence 3, and it'll have other uses&quot; v &quot;You must live longer than your lifespan would normally allow, and perfect your very being to the utmost degree to do so.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","user":"PlotVitalNPC","date":". 04-12-2018, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:13:21-07:00","id":1206039,"title":"","content":"The first thing to consider is, what would something like this add to your game? Personally I would generally be okay with that in my own campaigns as long as it's the unique result of some kind of epic transcendental event, access to unique artifacts or something similar. There probably wouldn't be more than a dozen such individuals I the world. This would help to show how Dragon Blooded can surpass their limitations and make them a little more interesting, and impressive, even if the examples are absolutely edge cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:26:34-07:00","id":1206042,"title":"","content":"The only DB with CCS was the Scarlet Empress because she has the Mantle of Brigid which allows its wearer to access one level greater of sorcery among other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:27:41-07:00","id":1206044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1206039#post1206039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing to consider is, what would something like this add to your game? Personally I would generally be okay with that in my own campaigns as long as it's the unique result of some kind of epic transcendental event, access to unique artifacts or something similar. There probably wouldn't be more than a dozen such individuals I the world. This would help to show how Dragon Blooded can surpass their limitations and make them a little more interesting, and impressive, even if the examples are absolutely edge cases.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That has been part of my premise this entire time.<br /> I've just also been suggesting the case of &quot;It shouldn't be transcendentally harder to develop a universal method for DBs to access that level than it was to do so for CMA, which is on the same tier. These are not contradictory, though, because developing a generalized method for CMA enlightenment seems to have been transcendentally difficult to begin with, and every subsequent method has just changed the bonus package the method offered.&quot;<br /> <br /> It adds the potential of a heroic and phenomenally unlikely journey for one of the DB CCSes - or perhaps a circle of them, formed by the members of that rarified group from all over creation, representing most of the actual amount of them, to seek the immense amount of resources and power needed to forge a universal method for it and cement the rule of the Terrestrial exalted over creation for thousands of years to come.<br /> <br /> Or something.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1206042#post1206042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only DB with CCS was the Scarlet Empress because she has the Mantle of Brigid which allows its wearer to access one level greater of sorcery among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of the canon facts - which I don't think have actually been reprinted since 1e. This is a thread about whether it breaks anything if you <i>change</i> that. I'd make the mantle of brigid something the empress <i>used</i> to achieve CCS, but only as part of her path to initiation, not the actual metaphysical source of it. IE, I'd make it 'just a mantle that Brigid wore, but that legend alone was enough for the empress to use as a symbolic ingredient or sacrifice for her own enlightenment'.<br /> <br /> The main <i>mostly </i><i>unaddressed </i>question here is &quot;Is it reasonable that, if one assumes all DBs have the technical capacity to reach beyond their station and grasp CCS, the thing holding them back is that nobody has found a way to collapse a deeply personal, epic, and heroic process of grasping that level into a pair of universally usable charms, as happened with CMA?&quot;, with the addendum that it's reasonable for such a method to be undiscovered because by 2e canon regarding how it happened, creating the first impersonal path to CMA seems to have been on the harder end of all projects ever accomplished. That's the part of my question that only two posts of the thread have attempted to address, with basically opposite responses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","user":"PlotVitalNPC","date":". 04-12-2018, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:08:44-07:00","id":1206061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1206044#post1206044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It shouldn't be transcendentally harder to develop a universal method for DBs to access that level than it was to do so for CMA, which is on the same tier. </div> </div> </div> </div>It's maybe worth keeping in mind that the basic concepts and themes of Martial Arts and Sorcery are very different. Just because you can standardize the process for one doesn't mean you can do so for the other. Ultimately they're not the same thing. <br /> <br /> Even if I allowed for a very, very tiny almost microscopic number of DB's with Celestial Circle Sorcery, each would have gotten that ability through a unique means that, explicitly, could not be replicated. They might be able to give advice or suggestions to other aspirants, but that's all, and it probably would not help all that much to be honest.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, Dragon Blooded <i>don't</i> have the innate capability of grasping CCS which means that any DB who <i>has</i> done so has managed to surpass their own Exaltation in the process, which is not something that can be calculated, quantified or standardized.<br /> <br /> I just think DBs using CCS would be incredibly disruptive if it was something that happened with any kind of real frequency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-12-2018, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:18:15-07:00","id":1206063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1206044#post1206044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of the canon facts - which I don't think have actually been reprinted since 1e. This is a thread about whether it breaks anything if you <i>change</i> that. I'd make the mantle of brigid something the empress <i>used</i> to achieve CCS, but only as part of her path to initiation, not the actual metaphysical source of it. IE, I'd make it 'just a mantle that Brigid wore, but that legend alone was enough for the empress to use as a symbolic ingredient or sacrifice for her own enlightenment'.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was in her writeup in Return of the Scarlet Empress. My comment while general also was specifically addressing other's comments that CSS might be accomplished with an Artifact. Given an artifact already exists that would be the base you work from.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would find CSS for a DB to be incredibly disruptive, and anything less than the Mantle would be out of the question. I think Akuma can get CSS too, so again, something on that scale fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T12:38:50-07:00","id":1206130,"title":"","content":"For one thing, Sidereals acting as faculty in the Heptagram wouldn't be nearly so sure that they could keep their students from spilling the beans. Given that the same problems would arise from teaching them a certain Sidereal style, I'm not sure why at least some Sidereals weren't decrying what Anys Syn was trying to do in training Myrrun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T10:42:30-07:00","id":1206521,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded able to freely summon demons of the second circle might have knock-on effects elsewhere that would have to be accounted for.<br /> <br /> I personally like the idea of DBs being able to perform CSS, but <i>only</i> in groups--it fits the theme that DBs are more powerful together and helps explain why it's rarer. If it were up to me, I might limit to the elemental-themed spells and require DBs of that aspect to perform the spell (so Fire aspects can cast Magma Kraken), but that makes it more of a plot device since it's unlikely any PC group will happen to match those limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Before enlightenment: chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment: Glorious Tree-Felling Prana and All-Encompassing Liquid-Carrying Methodology.","edited":{"userid":1223,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1223-dorchadas","user":"Dorchadas","date":". 04-17-2018, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1223-dorchadas","name":"Dorchadas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1223_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T03:15:33-07:00","id":1207209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1206042#post1206042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only DB with CCS was the Scarlet Empress because she has the Mantle of Brigid which allows its wearer to access one level greater of sorcery among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supposedly - don't know if it was ever confirmed she had the true Mantle and not a convincing fake. Convincing certain people of knowledge that you possess a certain achilles' heel one actually <b>does not</b> can be seen as sound strategic thinking.<br /> <br /> Truth be told afaik, there's not certainty even about her accessing the celestial circle through indirect means, instead of using a variety of resources with effects that might be mistaken for such, akin to Mnemon's limited but powerful access to more advanced summoning through the Emerald Thurible, for example.<br /> <br /> She could have the the true Mantle of Brigid, or learned the capacity through some secret technique of her own, or have a completely different and less notorious artifact that serves as true source of sorcerous puisance or her gifts hinge on the use of a dozen or more rare hearthstones, artifacts, charms &amp; spirit allies each depending on the occasion, among several other options. Overall the Empress is whatever is convenient to one's game and too much of a conundrum to serve as reliable example either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-15-2018, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T19:14:13-07:00","id":1207481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1207209#post1207209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Supposedly - don't know if it was ever confirmed she had the true Mantle and not a convincing fake.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said before, it's in her stat block which should be as objective as Exalted get on anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T19:48:39-07:00","id":1207490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1207481#post1207481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said before, it's in her stat block which should be as objective as Exalted get on anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>One more reason for me to be happy 2e is gone forever i guess...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T22:15:49-07:00","id":1207543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1205901-2e-would-it-break-the-setting-if-dbs-could-enlighten-into-ccs?p=1206063#post1206063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Akuma can get CSS too, so again, something on that scale fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dukantha had access to even some spells of the Solar Circle in the previous two editions, though I suspect that might not continue to be the case in a post-<i>MoEP:Infernals</i> version of the character.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T01:40:42-07:00","id":1207581,"title":"","content":"It's in her stat block in a non-canon scenario book. Unless you're actually running RotSE you can say that she wasn't wearing it when she disappeared or it randomly showed up somewhere or any number of other justifications to have someone else running around with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T02:36:49-07:00","id":1207591,"title":"","content":"One thing you might want to consider, is there is no standardized way to have a dragon blood initiate into Terrestrial sorcery. They have ways to help people pre disposed to learning sorcery to have a better chance to learn it but not a guaranteed way to do it. To have them standardize a way to Celestial Level would a significantly harder I imagine. Now that being said If it is something you want to do for your setting it sounds pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Like sending teams of Dragon blooded to pick up needed part from first age ruins to assemble a solar level working that a House is working on that would enable them to have the chance to take an existing Terrestrial level sorcerer and give them the same chance to learn Celestial Sorcery. (From the releases of the DB book so far I would recommend House Regara for this. They got the money and evidently the desire as well.) You could have the players be part of a team that is helping get the last parts to complete the working. Or you can have it already done too. Tons of ways to go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T10:57:04-07:00","id":1207707,"title":"","content":"So in short, my answer is &quot;Yes. In 2e, it fundamentally breaks the setting to allow any Terrestrial Exalt access to the Celestial Circle of Sorcery.&quot; The long answer is a version of &quot;Who cares. Do what's right for your table.<br /> <br /> So if your premise is that it was possible to mass produce Dragon-Blooded CC sorcerers all along, but no one bothered to do it, then you are, in theory approaching your game from the default setting point and then introducing this new discovery into the setting. That means you don't need to worry about things like &quot;why didn't the Realm conquer all of Creation with Celestial Circle sorcery.<br /> <br /> But this new discovery is going to have wide impact. It's going to start an arms race between the great houses. Lookshy is going to be scared about a Realm that's able to field large numbers of Celestial Circle Sorcerers. Lunars and Sidereals are going to be investigating whether the process can be scaled up so they can learn Solar Circle Sorcery (particularly Raski). And if the Empress Returns and she's not an Akuma, then she's no longer going to be to be one of 2 Celestial Circle Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> So there's alot of plot hooks that can come from this development. So yes, it absolutely &quot;breaks&quot; the setting, but there are quite a few different campaigns that can be fed from such a development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}